      "description": "The vigil demanding the release of seriously ill prisoners outside the Turkish Ministry of Justice in Ankara continues. On the fifth day, Tülay Hatimoğulları, Co-Chair of the Peoples’ Equality and Democracy Party (DEM Party), described the state’s treatment of sick prisoners as torture. She stated that prisoners were being denied timely medical treatment and prevented from being released despite suffering from life-threatening illnesses. The government must put an end to this practice, she said, referring to the ongoing peace and democratization process. Relatives of prisoners Ömer Güneri, Yakup Akman, Mehmet Ali Taşkın, and Selim Çiftçi were among those taking part in the vigil organized by",
